-- title:
--   $n=3$, p.25 (corrected: $(-2E_{12}+E_{13}+E_{23})/3$) — independent $\mathfrak{su}(2)$ on $\mathrm{DFS}_3(1/2)$
-- statement:
--   For three qubits:
--   1. exchange acts as $\mathfrak{su}$ independently on $\mathrm{DFS}_3(3/2)$ and $\mathrm{DFS}_3(1/2)$, at every legal $m$;
--   2. $\tfrac13(E_{12}+E_{13}+E_{23})$ is obtained from exchange, is the identity on the $J=3/2$ sector and vanishes on the $J=1/2$ sector ("$U(1)$ on $\mathrm{DFS}_3(3/2)$ alone");
--   3. $Z=\tfrac13(-2E_{12}+E_{13}+E_{23})$ and $X=\tfrac1{\sqrt3}(E_{13}-E_{23})$ belong to $H^3_{1/2}$: they are obtained from exchange, Hermitian, traceless, and vanish on the $J=3/2$ sector;
--   4. on $\mathrm{DFS}_3(1/2)$, at every legal $m$, they look like $\sigma_z$ and $\sigma_x$: there is an orthonormal pair $u,v$ there with $Zu=u$, $Zv=-v$, $Xu=v$, $Xv=u$.
--
--   This is the base case $n=3$ of the induction proving Theorem 5.
--
--   Differences from the source:
--   - correction: (7.19): ½(−E₁₂ + E₁₃ + E₂₃) = diag(0, 1, −1) → (1/3)(−2E₁₂ + E₁₃ + E₂₃), which is diag(0, 1, −1); reason: every E_ij is 1 on the J = 3/2 sector (e.g. on the all-|0⟩ state), so the printed combination is ½ there, not 0
--   - reading: any SU(2) gate on DFS_3(1/2); act independently on DFS_3(3/2) and DFS_3(1/2) → SectorUniversal 3 together with the explicit operators; reason: the Lie-algebra form of gate universality (p.11), the same form as the goal
--   - generalization: (7.18)–(7.19) in a fixed basis at a representative µ → every legal m, in an orthonormal pair of the DFS; reason: exchange does not depend on µ (p.24); the printed basis is one such pair
--   - generalization: Hamiltonians obtained by scalar multiplication, addition, Lie-commutator and unitary conjugation → i X in the real Lie algebra generated by the i E_ab (laws 1–3 only); reason: the smaller closure is contained in the printed one, so the Lean statement specializes to it; conjugation adds nothing (milestone (4.6))
--   - encoding: qubits 1, …, n; |0⟩, |1⟩ → 0-based wires Fin n; Bool basis with false = |0⟩; reason: Lean convention; same operators
--   - encoding: half-integer labels J, m → doubled labels j2 = 2J : ℕ, m2 = 2m : ℤ; reason: exact half-integers; same instances
-- source:
--   Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, Theory of Decoherence-Free Fault-Tolerant Universal Quantum Computation, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, eqs. (7.18)–(7.19) and the paragraph after them, p.25

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_CollectiveDFS_SectorUniversal

open QAlgorithms

namespace CollectiveDFS

/-- Theorem 5 at `n = 3`, §VII.C (Kempe, Bacon, Lidar & Whaley, arXiv:quant-ph/0004064v2, eqs. (7.18)–(7.19) and the paragraph after them, p.25, PDF
p.25): with `E_ij` the exchanges of three qubits,
(1) exchange acts as `su` independently on every `DFS_3(J)`, every legal `m`;
(2) `(E₁₂ + E₁₃ + E₂₃)/3` is obtained from exchange, is the identity on the `J = 3/2` sector and
zero on the `J = 1/2` sector ("U(1) on DFS_3(3/2) alone");
(3) `(−2E₁₂ + E₁₃ + E₂₃)/3` and `(E₁₃ − E₂₃)/√3` lie in `H^3_{1/2}`: obtained from exchange,
Hermitian, traceless, and zero on the `J = 3/2` sector;
(4) on `DFS_3(1/2)`, at every legal `m`, they "look like the Pauli σ_z and σ_x": there is an
orthonormal pair `u, v` in it with `Z u = u`, `Z v = −v`, `X u = v`, `X v = u`.

**Formalization Note** Wires 0-based: the paper's `E₁₂, E₁₃, E₂₃` are `exchange 0 1`,
`exchange 0 2`, `exchange 1 2`. Doubled labels: `J = 3/2, 1/2` are `3, 1`. Corrected: the
printed `½(−E₁₂+E₁₃+E₂₃)` of (7.19) is `½` on `J = 3/2`, not `0`. -/
theorem base_three :
    SectorUniversal 3 ∧
    Complex.I • ((1 / 3 : ℂ) • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2)) ∈
      exchangeLie 3 ∧
    (∀ ψ ∈ spinSector 3 3, Matrix.toEuclideanLin
      ((1 / 3 : ℂ) • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2)) ψ = ψ) ∧
    (∀ ψ ∈ spinSector 3 1, Matrix.toEuclideanLin
      ((1 / 3 : ℂ) • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2)) ψ = 0) ∧
    (1 / 3 : ℂ) • (-2 • exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2) ∈ sectorSet 3 1 ∧
    ((Real.sqrt 3 : ℂ))⁻¹ • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 2 - exchange 1 2) ∈ sectorSet 3 1 ∧
    (∀ m2 : ℤ, LegalM 1 m2 → ∃ u ∈ dfs 3 1 m2, ∃ v ∈ dfs 3 1 m2, Orthonormal ℂ ![u, v] ∧
      Matrix.toEuclideanLin
        ((1 / 3 : ℂ) • (-2 • exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2)) u = u ∧
      Matrix.toEuclideanLin
        ((1 / 3 : ℂ) • (-2 • exchange (0 : Fin 3) 1 + exchange 0 2 + exchange 1 2)) v = -v ∧
      Matrix.toEuclideanLin ((Real.sqrt 3 : ℂ)⁻¹ • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 2 - exchange 1 2)) u = v ∧
      Matrix.toEuclideanLin ((Real.sqrt 3 : ℂ)⁻¹ • (exchange (0 : Fin 3) 2 - exchange 1 2)) v =
        u) := by sorry

end CollectiveDFS
